<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib01622fa462d0bceda1e6041b5e3395ee7c2f94f" commit="893c727d93dfea96dae8b05e628dfa1e39634769" commit_message="vboot: Always compile vb2.1 stuff into utillib  Some of the vboot 2.0 and 2.1 functions call common code that currently lives inside the vb2.1 host library.  To be able to use vboot 2.0 code in futility, we always need to include the 2.1 sources.  BUG=chromium:611535 BRANCH=none TEST=make runtests  Change-Id: Ib01622fa462d0bceda1e6041b5e3395ee7c2f94f Signed-off-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356127 Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356127" owner_email="rspangler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/27/356127/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I176e7f424fa556d34d8fe691df5681f1e43210ce" commit="5341cd3f7dc5322e2ef49b23bf16173bb86dcdfb" commit_message="futility: Create signatures using vboot 2.0 APIs  Refactor futility to use only vboot 2.0 APIs to create signatures.  BUG=chromium:611535 BRANCH=none TEST=make runtests  Change-Id: I176e7f424fa556d34d8fe691df5681f1e43210ce Signed-off-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356128 Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356128" owner_email="rspangler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/28/356128/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2bd3f1d87acb069da0b56c1d7878e7d4fd6a06f3" commit="a7e041fa42818843f288721b576e67bfe2d7512a" commit_message="nrf51: Add Bluetooth LE support  RADIO_STATE is broken: remove it. Build on the geneneric radio support to send and receive Bluetooth LE packets. Add macros in registers.h to configure PCNF0 and PCNF1.  BUG=None BRANCH=None TEST=Send advertisements with console commands   ble_adv type length [interval_us]   for example: ble_adv 2 8   Advertisements should be received by other devices    The Bluetooth Address has the form C5:A4:A3:A2:A1:A*   The device name is a substring of ABCDEFGH...    ABCDEFGH @ C5:A4:A3:A2:A1:A2 (name length is 8, type is 2)   ABCDEFGH @ C5:A4:A3:A2:A1:A2 (name length is 8, type is 2)   ABCDEF   @ C5:A4:A3:A2:A1:A6 (name length is 6, type is 6) TEST=Listen for advertisements with console commands   ble_adv_scan chan [num] [addr0]   for example: ble_scan 37    Example output:    BLE packet @ 20000448: type 2, len 33,   5c.f3.70.6b.65.d2 AdvA    20000454: 02 01 08 17 09 43 68 72   2000045c: 6f 6d 65 62 6f 78 20 66   20000464: 6f 72 20 4d 65 65 74 69   2000046c: 6e 46 16    02 01 08 = 2 bytes, Flags, LE and BR capable   17 09 43... = 23 bytes, Name, &quot;Chromebox for Meetings&quot;  Change-Id: I2bd3f1d87acb069da0b56c1d7878e7d4fd6a06f3 Signed-off-by: Myles Watson &lt;mylesgw@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/361960 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Levi Oliver &lt;levio@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="361960" owner_email="mylesgw@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/60/361960/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idc12812fb88319ba6f8aad4396a175e3299211b8" commit="7ed74ebf55104f754f3a46f54eabb4c1cb18bd47" commit_message="nrf51: Add Bluetooth LE test code for the radio  Implement support for Direct Test Modet packets.  BUG=None BRANCH=None CQ-DEPEND=CL:361960 TEST=use hci commands to send and receive test packets.  Change-Id: Idc12812fb88319ba6f8aad4396a175e3299211b8 Signed-off-by: Myles Watson &lt;mylesgw@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362143 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Levi Oliver &lt;levio@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="362143" owner_email="mylesgw@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/43/362143/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.8" change_id="I5ddb2e6fe3a85a2cf030697cc9a5467f6b0ca237" commit="e2e0102c2a357081f5e0537d64027af8c71aaa88" commit_message="CHROMIUM: sysrq: replay the correct keys when releasing SysRq combo  When we changed SysRq code to terminate the SysRq state when releasing either Alt or SysRq (upstream allows releasing SysRq and only needing to keep pressing Alt) we neglected to adjust the event re-inject code which caused us to keep re-injecting Alt-SysRq combination every time SysRq alone was pressed until user again pressed and released Alt key.  Also we allowed F10 (Volume UP) to stand in for SysRq (since we do not have dedicated SysRq key on our keyboards) but re-inject code was not aware of this.  BUG=chromium:628508 TEST=1) Press Alt+Volume_Up (F10)      2) Release both      3) Press Volume_Up - OSD should show increased volume  Change-Id: I5ddb2e6fe3a85a2cf030697cc9a5467f6b0ca237 Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/361554 Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 7e7d95df29834784319b97f72360b75cd31a7eee  and resolved conflicts since we do not have support for reset sequence  in 3.8) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/364883 Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="364883" owner_email="dtor@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/83/364883/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5a0d2cadf90ff4a368d8fbeabf8e05795a31b5da" commit="b6c61ddfecad9bc8d0086c8a425ae27eafd65afa" commit_message="hostapd: Add a log message when stations PSK does not match.  BUG=None TEST=verified by attempting to connect a station with wrong PSK.  Change-Id: I5a0d2cadf90ff4a368d8fbeabf8e05795a31b5da Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/365840 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: John Walker &lt;walker@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="365840" owner_email="sduvvuri@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/hostap" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hostap" ref="refs/changes/40/365840/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If1d73fa7d90f6ac52fd1ab0ac563a6bf5fd10dc0" commit="b3a8c98f8ccb9ff24566ec454caf1b2b9866ef56" commit_message="reef: add pull-up for TCPC1 INT# when daughter board is not connected.  when the daughter board is not connected, TCPC1 INT# (USB_C1_PD_INT_ODL) will be floating since the external pull-up is located on the daughter board as well, and this floating signal will cause an interrupt storm and eventually cause a watchdog.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55488 BRANCH=none TEST=verify board no longer has watchdog reset when daughter baord      is not connected.  Change-Id: If1d73fa7d90f6ac52fd1ab0ac563a6bf5fd10dc0 Signed-off-by: Kevin K Wong &lt;kevin.k.wong@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/365499 Reviewed-by: Vijay P Hiremath &lt;vijay.p.hiremath@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="365499" owner_email="kevin.k.wong@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/99/365499/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icfc1fb634ca0f90cc98eede7acff2835c83f7e3f" commit="b9912d8a68d0e270794af02e5902fda0039f63fd" commit_message="Gale Board: Only set mac addr for EVT3 board and above  Exclude EVT1 variant with board ID 6.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55320 TEST=None BRANCH=None  Change-Id: Icfc1fb634ca0f90cc98eede7acff2835c83f7e3f Signed-off-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/365890 Reviewed-by: Julio Diez &lt;jdiez@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="365890" owner_email="kyan@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/90/365890/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I885cb92dbba1ca35f09404721fffa128b1f2fcbf" commit="b1485b53164ac628464682766c96450e3d8388e4" commit_message="Kefka: Add cras config files  Update EQ setting and volume tuning configuration for Kefka &amp; Sabin  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53142 TEST=Build image, write customization_id DELL-SABIN into VPD then check the volume configutaion applied  Change-Id: I885cb92dbba1ca35f09404721fffa128b1f2fcbf Signed-off-by: Ivy Jian &lt;ivy_jian@compal.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/365485 Reviewed-by: Mohammed Habibulla &lt;moch@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: YH Lin &lt;yueherngl@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jimmy Wang &lt;jimmym_wang@compal.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="365485" owner_email="ivy_jian@compal.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/85/365485/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I773c0138fd2243cdbcdd86b2c7138520155d7920" commit="06111efab7d35b596927e3b049b456f4ef744932" commit_message="g: Always reboot on watchdog or lockup  Watchdog events are delivered as internal ARM interrupts, so we can print a crash dump and then reboot. However, if interrupts are disabled when the watchdog triggers, it just hangs forever.  This CL configures the watchdog and processor lockup events to trigger a hard reboot through a security alert. This is the only way to make these events non-maskable.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52597 BRANCH=none TEST=manual  I added this console command:    static int command_hang(int argc, char **argv)   {    interrupt_disable();    while (1)     ;     return EC_ERROR_UNKNOWN; /* Not reached */   }   DECLARE_CONSOLE_COMMAND(hang, command_hang, NULL, &quot;Hang&quot;, NULL);  Without this CL, that command locked the SoC up until it was reset from outside. With this CL, it reboots after a couple of seconds.  Change-Id: I773c0138fd2243cdbcdd86b2c7138520155d7920 Signed-off-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/365531 Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="365531" owner_email="wfrichar@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/31/365531/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib6a414c0f4139fa523755ad7f29e593454570000" commit="de39b86be6a2044758fd421cae5a74900286c2ff" commit_message="lib/metrics.py: Added Queue indirection  When using multiprocessing in cbuildbot, we end up creating a duplicate ts_mon flushing thread. The parent and child threads may end send conflicting messages. Furthermore, messages from the child may not be sent if the child process finishes before its thread flushes messages. To solve this, we add an &quot;indirect&quot; flag to SetupTsMonGlobalState, which creates a multiprocessing.Queue. The parent and child send metrics to the Queue, and a separate process consumes these messages and emits metrics via ts_mon.  BUG=chromium:623293 TEST=cbuildbot binhost-pre-cq -p chromiumos/chromite --local  Change-Id: Ib6a414c0f4139fa523755ad7f29e593454570000 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/363502 Commit-Ready: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="363502" owner_email="phobbs@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="11" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/02/363502/11" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8809d7425bdaf6406d3c9c190bd3d6265e68e1cb" commit="88df7cb293cae9eb40667100dd81acf56e0f6e81" commit_message="trunks: fix const definition checks in generator unittest  BUG=none TEST=generator/generator_test.py returns OK  Change-Id: I8809d7425bdaf6406d3c9c190bd3d6265e68e1cb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/365947 Commit-Ready: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="365947" owner_email="apronin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="aosp/platform/system/tpm" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/tpm" ref="refs/changes/47/365947/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib065e6b0186772a611ee312c0fb99cc5c2b84c01" commit="ea436c6703353355ac0269409f71caba87e499d4" commit_message="dev-go/fsnotify: add File system notifications for Go  Use github.com/fsnotify/fsnotify as the source repository. Following instruction at https://www.chromium.org/chromium-os/developer-guide/go-in-chromium-os  TEST=&quot;FEATURES=test emerge-whirlwind dev-go/fsnotify&quot; pass. Built program      calls fsnotify to watch for directory and file changes, tested pass. BUG=b:30498724  Change-Id: Ib065e6b0186772a611ee312c0fb99cc5c2b84c01 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/364380 Commit-Ready: Zhihong Yu &lt;zhihongyu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Zhihong Yu &lt;zhihongyu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rahul Chaudhry &lt;rahulchaudhry@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="364380" owner_email="zhihongyu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/80/364380/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I897e453296151f31344f3e0434202baa67c7025d" commit="4266f9da52507b4194bfbca8ad45b35dfac39aeb" commit_message="reef: Add code to read battery temperature  Reef doesn't have the battery temperature sense pin connected to the charger, hence reading the battery temperature from the battery registers.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55834 BRANCH=none TEST=Using 'battery' &amp; 'temps' console command verified,      temperature readings are same from both the commands.  Change-Id: I897e453296151f31344f3e0434202baa67c7025d Signed-off-by: Vijay Hiremath &lt;vijay.p.hiremath@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/365970 Commit-Ready: Vijay P Hiremath &lt;vijay.p.hiremath@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Vijay P Hiremath &lt;vijay.p.hiremath@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="365970" owner_email="vijay.p.hiremath@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/70/365970/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7f06baea394aff4f9ace393b69bc20a1d0a4ad10" commit="1c541719595153b4a8b41737fca4a39eccdc5e40" commit_message="hostapd: Clean up event messages sent to control interface.  On ctrl_interface event messages: 1. Print separator before each field instead of after. 2. Print steering_reason as a string instead of a code. 3. Add defer delta time to nosteer deferred messages (AP_STA_NO_STEERING and appropriate AP_STA_ASSOC). 4. Add probe_delta value to AP_STA_NO_STEERING events 5. Add probe_delta and steer_delta values to AP_STA_STEERING events 6. Add rssi and steer_delta values to nosteer &quot;recently-steered&quot; events. Fix memory leak when sending control interface event messages.  BUG=b:30605166 BUG=b:30604423 BUG=b:30604430 BUG=b:30606008 BUG=b:30640571 TEST=Verify messages are properly handled by event upload code.  Change-Id: I7f06baea394aff4f9ace393b69bc20a1d0a4ad10 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/365512 Commit-Ready: John Walker &lt;walker@google.com&gt; Tested-by: John Walker &lt;walker@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="365512" owner_email="walker@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/hostap" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hostap" ref="refs/changes/12/365512/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibd7624ad8e3b4126f6346dce0bc72f62a3cc6d18" commit="59e9f8bc14931d6c51e0c3dbef1f8b23db2646cd" commit_message="Cr50: Sample slave configuration pins at POR  There is just one version of Cr50 firmware for all boards that it's used on. However, on some boards the AP communicates to the TPM via a SPI interface (i.e. Kevin) and on others, the AP communicates via an I2C interface (i.e. Reef). In order to dynamically discover which interface to configure, there are strapping resistors added to the board which enables the Cr50 to detect which configuration to implement.  This CL is a first pass and is only looking at DIOA1 which is pulled high for SPI and pulled low for I2C configurations. The strapping resistor should be read when the AP is in reset prior to it attempting to drive any of the lines used for strapping. To ensure this condition is met, Cr50 will only check the strapping options following a POR (power on reset). Once the configuration type is discovered, a 'long_life' register is used to hold the result so that the result can always be available. The long_life register contents remain unchanged until a subsequent power down event.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:50728 TEST=manual Tested on Kevin and Reef. Verfifed by reading the stored value that the SPI configuraiton is detected for Kevin and the I2C interface is detected on Reef. In addition, verified on Kevin that the Cr50 FW version is correctly reported to the AP which means that TPM register reads via the slave SPI are functioning.  Change-Id: Ibd7624ad8e3b4126f6346dce0bc72f62a3cc6d18 Signed-off-by: Scott &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/363014 Commit-Ready: Scott Collyer &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Scott Collyer &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="363014" owner_email="scollyer@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/14/363014/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia69138a2247b0ed03074506a1f58fbd2418ae533" commit="319093387699f003f80ca52e536e3d0a82a15f35" commit_message="Change ebuild to reflect the move of CFM client tests to server  CFM santiy and session stress test were moved from client to server, hence changing the ebuild files to reflect this change.  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: Ia69138a2247b0ed03074506a1f58fbd2418ae533 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/365530 Commit-Ready: Harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="365530" owner_email="harpreet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/30/365530/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4b7174829b3926d771e555654605d7c84ecd4ec4" commit="43fdd79eb7f1a27749dcf46ce093e68adbc9b33d" commit_message="Migrate CFM volume change test to server using cfm_facade  Move CFM volume change test to server using cfm_facade to execute the needed telemetry commands from server side.  BUG=None TEST=Tested on a local DUT setup.  Change-Id: I4b7174829b3926d771e555654605d7c84ecd4ec4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/365504 Commit-Ready: Harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="365504" owner_email="harpreet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/04/365504/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><lkgm version="8670.0.0-rc3"/></manifest>